SUMMARY:Appalachian Frights and Bumps in the Night
DESCRIPTION:An evening of spooky mountain tales with storyteller Adam Booth \nJoin Adam Booth\, the 2022 West Virginia Folk Artist of the Year\, as he shares a program of seasonally spooky stories from the heart of Appalachia. Adam will take you on a journey to the deepest dark hollers\, sharing traditional stories of haints\, witches\, and dreadful omens in the night. \nThis program is free and open to the public. (Please note: These stories are aimed at adults rather than small children.) \nThank you to the Madison County Tourism Development Authority for their support of this event.
URL:https://www.mhu.edu/event/appalachian-frights-and-bumps-in-the-night/
LOCATION:Owen Theatre\, 44 College St\, Mars Hill\, 28754\, United States
CATEGORIES:Appalachian Studies,Cultural Events,Featured,RAMSEYCENTER
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.mhu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/appfrights1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Ramsey Center for Appalachian Studies":MAILTO:lweinstein@mhu.edu
END:VEVENT
